Also, for the duplicate check we need to track which ids have been seen among *valid* preceding bookings? Preceding bookings were fully validated at their turn, so all preceding bookings are valid. Keep a Set of ids as we go.

4. R4: overlap within the same room, [start, end) semantics. Conflict when startA < endB && startB < endA.

5. R5: pairs [idA, idB] with idA < idB (string comparison). Sorted by idA, then idB.

Wait — "with `idA < idB` in the usual string comparison". Interesting: ids are arbitrary strings, so the pair is sorted by id string, not by array order. So for any conflicting pair of bookings with ids x and y, output [min(x,y), max(x,y)] by string comparison. Then sort all pairs by idA, then idB.

